Here  you  can  include  any  attempts  that  have  been  made  to  tackle  the  issues  discussed  in  the 
“Background Information” section of your Study Guide. It is not necessary to include all attempts to 
solve the issue, but you should definitely mention some that you deem important for the topic. 
Describe each attempt, the extent of and the reasons behind their success (or lack thereof). 
Possible Solutions 
This is the most important section of your Study Guide. The solutions and approaches that you 
present  to  provide  an  effective  resolution  to  this topic will  be  used  by  the  delegates  in  their 
preparation. You should not “give away” the solutions to the issue but give the delegates room to 
think  and  develop  the  ideas  provided  in  this  section,  as  well  as  suggest  areas  to  explore  when 
researching on their own. 
Further reading (optional) 
A list of useful articles, reports, videos, or anything that delegates can use as a starting point to 
conduct their own research. The resources provided here should complement your Study Guide, not 
replace it. Focus on quality, over quantity, and prefer websites and links that can actually help the 
delegates. 
This section is optional, but it is highly recommended that you include it. 
References and Bibliography 
Every claim, statistic, or piece of vital information if your Study Guide should be backed by a source. 
Include a formatted list of all sources in your Study Guide here. 
General Remarks 
1. Delete this section, as well as the main text of all sections within this template, before you start 
writing your Study Guide 
2. All references, bibliographic mentions, citations and footnotes should be in the APA7 format. 
It is recommended that you use a citation manager like MyBib or Zotero to keep track of your 
sources. 
3. The general formatting guidelines for this Study Guide have as follows: 
a. Font: Palatino Linotype (16px for Heading 1, 11px for Headings 2&3 and Main Text) 
b. Line Spacing: 1.20 
c. Paragraph Spacing: 16pt Before for Heading 1, 12pt After for Headings 2&3 and Main 
Text 
d. Text justification: Justify (full line) 
e. Footnotes: Palatino Linotype (10px, Line Spacing: 1) 
4. Plagiarism and the use of Artificial Intelligence Models during the writing process of this 
Study Guide are strictly forbidden. Remember to appropriately cite your sources! 